    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field following the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (`Owner` schema) \u2014 added a `readOnly` `initials` string property alongside `displayName`. The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.initials` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing the value:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n   This upper-cases the first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot \u2014 e.g. `\"john\"` + `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` response already serializes `OwnerDto` via `RespondWithOwner`, so `$.initials` is now returned. `./mvnw test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
